  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Gen AI for Gen Z: Inspiring new generation of AI creators</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Despite growing excitement about AI, Cambodia faces low understanding and experience in applying these powerful tools. The need to address biases and ethical AI use early is crucial for responsible applications. Currently, only 10% of Cambodian students choose IT fields, creating a significant gap in the country&apos;s AI readiness.&quot;GenAI for Gen Z&quot; is a unique educational program designed to target Cambodian youth, ensuring at least 50% female participation. This project will introduce the transformative power of Generative AI, sparking a shift within Cambodian students. By bringing diverse genders together, we foster open discussions and understanding. We 
specifically target students from social and humanitarian sciences&#x2014;particularly women&#x2014;to inspire them with AI&apos;s potential, unleashing new possibilities for collaboration and creative applications.
As a leader in innovation and STEM support, the UK can play a pivotal role in fostering Cambodia&apos;s AI future. Funding this project helps bridge a knowledge gap, promotes inclusivity and responsible AI development, empowers underrepresented students, and inspires a new generation of tech creators in Cambodia. This investment aligns directly with the UK&apos;s goals of promoting technological leadership and global collaboration, as well as the principles laid out in the Bletchley Declaration for fostering public trust and confidence in AI systems.</narrative>
  </description>
